# Build/dev artifacts -- never useful inside the image
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/

# Real bug fixed: this Dockerfile serves the Streamlit app
# (dashboard/app.py) only -- it never needs the Next.js frontend
# (Partie 8+) or any SDK's own node_modules/build output at all.
# Left un-excluded, `frontend/node_modules/` and `frontend/.next/`'s
# own binary Turbopack cache made the build context huge enough to
# fail outright ("read-only file system" while writing the overlay
# snapshot -- a real, reproducible failure, not a fluke).
#
# Second real bug fixed (2026-09-17): .dockerignore is shared across
# EVERY Dockerfile that builds from this context, not just the
# Streamlit one above -- a blanket `frontend/` exclusion here also hid
# `frontend/widget/` from Dockerfile.api's own COPY (added the same
# day), breaking the Render build outright ("/frontend/widget": not
# found) despite the directory being real and committed. A `!frontend/widget/`
# negation was tried first and rejected: Docker's own documented
# .dockerignore behavior is that once a parent directory is excluded,
# files under it can't be re-included by a later negation pattern --
# so instead of excluding all of frontend/ and trying to carve an
# exception back out, only the specific large/build-only subdirectories
# that caused the original bug are excluded below, by name.
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/.next/
frontend/coverage/
sdks/*/node_modules/
sdks/*/dist/
sdks/python/*.egg-info/

# Version control and CI, not runtime
.git/
.github/

# Secrets -- must never be baked into an image layer
.env
.streamlit/secrets.toml

# Derived/local-only data -- chroma is rebuilt on first run from the
# committed data/processed/fastapi_docs.json; raw docs are a gitignored
# copy of another repo and aren't needed once data/processed exists
data/chroma/
data/raw/

# Not needed at runtime
tests/
AUDIT.md
calibration/
